WEBVTT

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:08.460
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Wednesday the 25th. Can you all hear me?</v>

00:00:09.859 --> 00:00:13.710
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah. Am I coming through all right? Bit noisy this end.</v>

00:00:14.119 --> 00:00:17.269
<v David Whitfield>You're fine. There's a sort of humming behind you.</v>

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.949
<v Tomasz Nowak>That's the fan, not me. Haven't had enough coffee to hum.</v>

00:00:24.949 --> 00:00:27.750
<v Callum Reid>Same. Kettle's taking longer than the shift handover.</v>

00:00:29.839 --> 00:00:33.689
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, no Jamie Brennan or Priya Raman today. Just us six.</v>

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:40.789
<v Hannah Price>Before we get into it, the charity bake sale on Friday — apparently there's proper competition over the brownies.</v>

00:00:43.049 --> 00:00:45.850
<v Marcus Hale>Competition as in baking them or eating them?</v>

00:00:48.179 --> 00:00:51.329
<v Hannah Price>Baking. You'd win the other one without much opposition.</v>

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:59.340
<v Sarah Okafor>Ha. Anyone got weekend plans that don't involve eating? We were thinking of a walk, but the weather looks grim.</v>

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:03.990
<v David Whitfield>A walk to the pub still counts in the rain.</v>

00:01:05.099 --> 00:01:08.599
<v Callum Reid>Forecast changes every time I open it. I've stopped looking.</v>

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:15.340
<v Sarah Okafor>Probably sensible. Right, Tom, how are the bits from the earlier stand-ups going?</v>

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:19.640
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, so I've made a start on the monthly test.</v>

00:01:21.579 --> 00:01:26.129
<v Tomasz Nowak>And the seals on the GT2 inlet valve, I'm about halfway through those.</v>

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:28.230
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, cheers.</v>

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:34.730
<v Hannah Price>The contractor booking for the GT2 Inlet Water Injection Valve is sorted, by the way. All fine.</v>

00:01:36.609 --> 00:01:37.810
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely, thanks.</v>

00:01:39.859 --> 00:01:44.409
<v David Whitfield>And I signed off the inspection on the number two bearing on Tuesday.</v>

00:01:44.719 --> 00:01:47.519
<v Callum Reid>Tuesday? Sorry, the days are merging a bit.</v>

00:01:49.719 --> 00:01:51.469
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, yesterday. All signed off.</v>

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:55.530
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, onto the new stuff, then.</v>

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:59.969
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll run a function test on the pop valve by Thursday.</v>

00:02:00.689 --> 00:02:05.239
<v Marcus Hale>That's you on the pop valve then, Saz? Sorry, you clipped a bit.</v>

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:10.289
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, me. I'll have the function test done by Thursday.</v>

00:02:12.509 --> 00:02:17.759
<v Tomasz Nowak>I'll inspect the big valve by the gate for leaks, as well. Tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:20.840
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Tom. Normal priority on that?</v>

00:02:23.289 --> 00:02:26.439
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, normal priority. Tomorrow at 9:30 for the inspection.</v>

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:30.689
<v Callum Reid>Tomorrow's Thursday, isn't it? Honestly, ignore me.</v>

00:02:31.509 --> 00:02:35.710
<v Tomasz Nowak>It is. We could put the days on the kettle for you.</v>

00:02:37.319 --> 00:02:41.169
<v Sarah Okafor>Cal, can you write up the near miss at the Palletiser?</v>

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:45.199
<v Callum Reid>Yeah — when do you need the write-up in?</v>

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:55.289
<v Sarah Okafor>On the 3rd, but that one's safety critical, straight away. I need you starting on it now, not waiting till the 3rd.</v>

00:02:56.710 --> 00:03:03.009
<v Callum Reid>Understood. I'll start straight away and get the near miss at the Palletiser written up on the 3rd.</v>

00:03:04.259 --> 00:03:08.460
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, not one to leave sitting at the bottom of an inbox.</v>

00:03:10.889 --> 00:03:12.090
<v Callum Reid>No, absolutely.</v>

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:15.349
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Cal.</v>

00:03:16.719 --> 00:03:21.620
<v Marcus Hale>And I'll do the pre-use checks on the Forklift Fleet tomorrow morning. Normal priority.</v>

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:27.560
<v Callum Reid>Sorry, spoke over you there, Marc. You said pre-use checks?</v>

00:03:29.389 --> 00:03:34.289
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll do the pre-use checks on the Forklift Fleet. Normal priority, tomorrow morning.</v>

00:03:36.689 --> 00:03:37.889
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Marc.</v>

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:42.830
<v David Whitfield>Teams just froze on me. Was there something after that?</v>

00:03:44.219 --> 00:03:46.669
<v Sarah Okafor>No, just me saying thanks to Marc.</v>

00:03:47.169 --> 00:03:50.319
<v David Whitfield>Right, good. Everyone went very thoughtful for a second.</v>

00:03:50.789 --> 00:03:54.639
<v Hannah Price>That's just our faces before nine. Mine's thinking about Friday's cake.</v>

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:58.879
<v Tomasz Nowak>At least it's for charity. Makes the second slice practically compulsory.</v>

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:02.689
<v Callum Reid>That's the sort of technical argument I can support.</v>

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:09.370
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes a cake meeting — anything else relevant? Nothing more from me.</v>

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:12.560
<v David Whitfield>Nothing else here.</v>

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:15.310
<v Tomasz Nowak>No, that's me.</v>

00:04:17.399 --> 00:04:18.800
<v Marcus Hale>All good here too.</v>

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:21.970
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Thanks, everyone. Catch you on the floor.</v>
